{:preamble "Gum is a set of optional Wattle modules. The runtime does not load them.
            Naming a module copies it and its licence into deps/gum in the current
            directory, and --dir sets a different directory to hold gum. A file in the
            project imports the copy by its relative path:

              (import ./deps/gum/args :as args)

            Modules:"
 :modules
 [{:name "args"
   :files ["args.wattle" "LICENSE.argy-bargy"]
   :help "Parses command-line arguments against a config of options, parameters and subcommands, and formats the usage text. It is a port of Argy-Bargy."}
  {:name "test"
   :files ["test.wattle" "LICENSE.testament"]
   :help "Defines tests with deftest, checks them with is and runs them with run-tests!, which reports the failures. wattle test runs the files that use it. It is a port of Testament."}]}
